format_webm: avoid pointer arithmetic on void *

copy_possible() offsets its void * arguments before handing them to memcpy.
Adding to a void * is a GCC extension; the Visual C++ compiler rejects it
(error C2036: 'void *': unknown size) and has no switch to allow it. The file
cannot simply be left out either: shout.c calls shout_open_webm()
unconditionally.

Cast both operands to char * for the arithmetic, which is what the extension
means anyway. Upstream has no Windows build, so nothing there hits this.

--- a/src/format_webm.c
+++ b/src/format_webm.c
@@ -437,7 +437,7 @@

     if (target_space < to_copy) to_copy = target_space;

-    memcpy(target_base + *target_position, src_base + *src_position, to_copy);
+    memcpy((char *)target_base + *target_position, (const char *)src_base + *src_position, to_copy);

     *src_position += to_copy;
     *target_position += to_copy;
